   <p>NEPSE operates on Nepal Standard Time (NST), which is UTC+5:45 — one of the few time zones in the world not aligned to a full or half hour, a quirk of Nepal's geography relative to India. The trading day is shorter than that of most major international exchanges, running from Sunday through Thursday (Nepal's working week), reflecting the country's official five-day working schedule.</p>
