   <p>Having walked through banking, hydropower, insurance, and manufacturing separately, the practical task for a Nepali investor holding — or considering — positions across more than one of these sectors is to build a mental (or literal, in a spreadsheet) benchmark table that lets you judge each stock against its own sector's realistic range, not against a single NEPSE-wide number that does not actually exist for any of them.</p>
