     <tr><td>Capacity (MW)</td><td>Maximum instantaneous output</td><td>Sets the ceiling on possible revenue</td></tr>
     <tr><td>Capacity factor</td><td>Actual output as a percent of the ceiling</td><td>River hydrology and reliability shrink revenue below the ceiling</td></tr>
     <tr><td>PPA tariff (wet/dry)</td><td>Contracted price per unit sold to NEA</td><td>Determines revenue per unit generated</td></tr>
@@ -13165,7 +14481,7 @@
   <p>Putting both hemispheres together gives us Upper Tamakoshi's real, current Canon Score.</p>
   <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
   <table class="figures">
-    <tr><th>Canon Score dimension</th><th>Sub-score</th><th>Out of</th><th>What drove it</th></tr>
+    <tr><th scope="col">Canon Score dimension</th><th scope="col">Sub-score</th><th scope="col">Out of</th><th scope="col">What drove it</th></tr>
     <tr><td>Liquidity &amp; Tradability</td><td>7</td><td>10</td><td>Large-cap, fully public float, but a cooling price trend</td></tr>
     <tr><td>Governance &amp; Promoter Behaviour</td><td>11</td><td>15</td><td>Credible state sponsor, no misconduct, but a five-time-delayed, 154%-overrun execution record</td></tr>
