   <p>The final and perhaps most consequential lesson of this chapter is behavioural rather than mechanical. Retail investors in NEPSE consistently make three related errors around policy events, and each is a direct consequence of misunderstanding the transmission lag documented above rather than of any failure to read the policy correctly on its own terms.</p>
