   <h3>The Ownership Structure</h3>
   <p>Nepal Stock Exchange Ltd. is not a purely private institution. It is a government-controlled company in which multiple state entities hold significant stakes. Understanding this ownership structure explains much about NEPSE's regulatory culture, its pace of technological modernisation, its relationship with listed companies, and the inherent conflicts of interest embedded in its operation.</p>
