     Do not treat any cell in this table as a price target, a floor, or a ceiling. A sector trading below its historical bear-phase range is not automatically cheap, and a sector trading above its historical bull-phase range is not automatically overheated — it may simply mean the range itself has shifted, or that something in the underlying business (a capital raise, a regulatory change, an earnings distortion) explains the number better than sentiment does. Use this table to ask better questions, not to skip asking them.
