   <p>The discipline that keeps a personal Canon Score model useful for fifteen years, the way Rajendra's has stayed useful, is not vigilance in the sense of constant monitoring. It is a fixed, boring, once-a-year (plus one light mid-year pass) routine that takes an afternoon and catches the changes that matter before they cause a mistake. Trying to track every announcement as it happens is exhausting and unnecessary for a retail investor who is not trading on regulatory news. A calendar-based refresh is enough.</p>
