   <h3>What Wash Trading Is</h3>
   <p>Wash trading is the practice of simultaneously buying and selling the same security between connected parties — or by the same party using different accounts — with the result that no real change in ownership occurs but transaction volume is artificially inflated. The trades 'wash' against each other. The economic content of such trades is zero, but their appearance in the public trading record creates the impression of activity, interest, and liquidity that does not actually exist.</p>
