   <h3>Underwriting and Its Implications</h3>
   <p>Many IPOs in Nepal are underwritten, meaning the underwriter guarantees to purchase any shares not subscribed by the public. Underwriting sounds like a safety net, but it is worth questioning why an underwriter agreed to guarantee the issue. Underwriters are professional investors — if they were genuinely uncertain about demand, they would charge a very high underwriting premium or decline entirely. An underwritten IPO at a reasonable premium suggests the IM is confident in minimum demand. An IPO that struggles to find underwriters is a warning signal.</p>
