   <h3>The Regulatory Ecosystem</h3>
   <p>Mutual funds in Nepal operate under the Mutual Fund Regulations, 2010 issued by the Securities Board of Nepal (SEBON). All fund management companies (FMCs) must be licensed by SEBON and must appoint a separate depositary — typically a commercial bank — to hold the fund's assets in custody. This two-entity structure (FMC + depositary) provides an important layer of investor protection: the fund manager never directly holds the assets, reducing fraud risk.</p>
