   <h3>The Practical Guidance</h3>
   <p>A disciplined investor should, before committing capital to any Nepali mutual fund scheme, explicitly calculate the total cost of ownership — combining the AER, any applicable loads, and an estimate of transaction cost drag from portfolio turnover. This number should be weighed against the fund's realistic gross return potential given its mandate. If the cost of active management equals or exceeds the realistic alpha generation, an investor would rationally prefer a lower-cost vehicle if one is available.</p>
