   <p>Interest income from government bonds and savings bonds is subject to withholding tax, though specific rates and exemptions have varied over time and have been modified through successive Finance Acts. Investors should verify the applicable tax treatment at the time of purchase rather than relying on historical precedent. For tax-exempt or tax-advantaged funds — provident funds, pension funds — government securities are particularly attractive because the gross yield translates more fully into net return than it would for a taxable investor.</p>
