     <span class="callout-label">WARNING</span>
     Some hydropower companies have been observed continuing to capitalise costs, including certain operating expenses incurred during an extended "trial run" or testing period after physical completion, beyond what NFRS would strictly permit, in order to defer expense recognition and present a stronger pre-commercial-operation profit picture to prospective bonus/rights subscribers. An investor should treat an unusually long gap between a hydropower company's announced physical completion date and its declared commercial operation date as worth investigating through the notes on capitalised borrowing cost and capital work-in-progress.
