     A bank whose reported NPL ratio is flat or improving while its provisioning coverage ratio is falling and its "loans and advances to related parties or group companies" note is silent or minimal is showing the classic signature of an evergreened book: stress is being hidden through reclassification and restructuring rather than resolved through recovery or write-off.
