   <p>For a bank, the balance sheet's defining asset is the loan book. For a manufacturer or trading company, it is inventory. Nepal Accounting Standard 2 — Inventories (NAS 2, converged with IAS 2) governs how these companies value the single largest working-capital line on their balance sheets, and it is worth learning its mechanics precisely because errors or aggressive judgment calls here flow directly into reported gross margin.</p>
