   <p>The final lesson of this sector, and in many ways of this entire Part, is one of humility about comparability. Manufacturing, trading, and hotels are where NEPSE offers you the fewest peers, the thinnest disclosure norms, and the heaviest reliance on family-group context — which means the analytical rigor you bring to reading a single company's inventory note, working capital trend, and related-party disclosure matters more here, not less, than in the crowded and standardised sectors that dominate the rest of the exchange.</p>
