   <p>Everything described so far — the rate table, the WACC pool, the bonus and rights adjustments — culminates in a single automated event: the moment your sell order settles, typically on T+2 (two business days after the trade date), the broker's Trading Management System (TMS), working through CDSC's clearing infrastructure, computes the gain, applies the correct rate, deducts the tax, and credits you only the net amount. You do not write a cheque to the IRD. You do not calculate anything yourself unless you are checking the broker's work.</p>
