   <p>With this chapter, Part VII's taxation survey is complete: across three prior chapters and this one, you have moved from understanding what NEPSE taxes are and how they are calculated, to what this chapter has tried to give you — a working discipline for legally minimising what you pay without ever crossing into evasion, misrepresentation, or wishful readings of provisions that say something more modest than market folklore claims. Part VII now turns from taxation to ratios — from what the state takes to what the numbers on a company's own financial statements can tell you about what it is actually worth keeping.</p>
