     <span class="callout-label">CASE IN POINT</span>
     Chilime Hydropower Company, a 22.1 MW plant on the Chilime Khola in Rasuwa district and one of NEA's earliest subsidiary companies, is often cited as Nepal's pioneering project-company model — an NEA-controlled SPV that later opened its shares to the general public and local Rasuwa residents specifically, well before hydropower IPOs became a routine NEPSE listing pathway. It set an early template that many subsequent Nepali hydropower SPVs — offering a fixed local-resident share quota alongside public and promoter tranches — have followed.
