   <p>A score is a starting point for judgment, not a replacement for it. Two companies can both score 75 for very different reasons — one strong everywhere and merely adequate on valuation, another spectacular on growth but only middling on governance. Always read the seven sub-scores before you read the total, exactly as Suman read Kavita's Mathematics grade before he looked at her GPA.</p>
