   <p>Before any decision can be made well, the facts have to be assembled in one place. This is the least glamorous step in the entire rights-issue playbook, and it is also the one investors skip most often — scrolling past the notice, noting only "oh, rights shares," and moving on without ever reading the numbers that actually determine whether participating makes sense.</p>
