   <p>Let's now do the exercise this whole case study has been building toward: apply the Canon Score and the risk-management rules from earlier in this book to my own actual decisions in 2021, and see, point by point, where a disciplined process would have produced a different outcome — not a perfect outcome, since no process eliminates risk entirely, but a materially better one. Because this case study is about a whole market rather than one company, there is no single ticker to run Chapter 64's real seven-dimension rubric against. So, in the same spirit as Chapter 64's own illustrative "Himalaya Unnati Bank" composite, here is a numeric Canon Score for a composite that stood in for dozens of real names in 2021: a small, single-plant hydropower developer of exactly the kind that kept hitting upper circuit in Kathmandu's tea-shop conversations that year, built from the real, aggregate conditions this chapter has already documented — thin disclosure, heavy project debt, a single-buyer PPA, and a share price disconnected from any of it.</p>
