   <p>This is the eighth of eleven full case studies that make up Part XVI of this Canon, and the first to step back from a single company to look at the whole market at once. Across mergers, frauds, currency shocks, sector collapses, and now a full national mania and correction, the aim of every case study has been the same: to take the individual tools built up across the rest of this book and show them working, or failing to work, in real events with real numbers, lived through by people not so different from you. Three case studies remain: a hydropower project's own cost and schedule overrun, an insurance company's claims and solvency picture, and a hotel operator's fortunes through a real, recent shock to Nepali tourism — each one carrying every lesson from this part of the book forward into a different corner of the market.</p>
