   <p>Theory is easiest to absorb through a complete example. Meet our fictional narrator for this lesson: Sunita Adhikari, a 32-year-old schoolteacher in Pokhara. She has been investing in NEPSE for four years, started with a small inheritance and a habit of saving from her monthly salary, and has just finished reading Chapters 90 through 95 of this book. She sits down on a quiet Saturday and writes the following document. It is not perfect, and it is not meant to be copied word for word — it is meant to show you the shape, the tone, and the level of specificity a real constitution should have.</p>
   <p>Sunita Adhikari's Investment Constitution — Written Baisakh 2082, to be reviewed every Baisakh thereafter.</p>
