     A drawdown rulebook that exists only in your head is not a rule. It is a mood. Write it down, date it, and store it somewhere you will actually look during a crisis — a notes app, a printed page in a folder, a message to yourself. The entire value of a pre-committed rule comes from its being harder to quietly revise than a thought you had while the market was calm.
